theory.intro:
Pythagoras' theorem links the three sides of a right-angled triangle. Stating it correctly, in symbols and in words, is what every later Pythagoras calculation relies on.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0,2.4);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$b$};
\draw (A)--(C) node[midway,left] {$a$};
\draw (C)--(B) node[midway,above right] {$h$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(A)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

facts:
The letters are only labels: if the hypotenuse is called $r$, the theorem is $p^2+q^2=r^2$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0,2.4);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$q$};
\draw (A)--(C) node[midway,left] {$p$};
\draw (C)--(B) node[midway,above right] {$r$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(A)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Write Pythagoras' theorem for this right-angled triangle.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (R) at (0,2);
\coordinate (S) at (-2,0);
\coordinate (T) at (2,0);
\draw (R)--(S)--(T)--cycle;
\draw (-0.212132,1.787868)--(0,1.575736)--(0.212132,1.787868);
\path (R)--(S) node[midway,above left] {$b$};
\path (R)--(T) node[midway,above right] {$c$};
\path (S)--(T) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A student writes $k^2+m^2=j^2$ for this right-angled triangle. Explain the error and write the correct equation.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0,2.4);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$j$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,left] {$k$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$m$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
